course: dictionary
lesson: 7403
title: Poet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A poet is a person who writes poems. Poems often play with sound and pictures, so a poet chooses words carefully for how they sound and what they show.
explain: «Poets paint pictures with words» is a clue: a poet paints with words, not with a brush. To do this, poets use tricks such as the simile, the metaphor, personification and alliteration.
explain: Some poems rhyme and have a regular beat, but «Free verse has no regular rhyme or beat» and it is still poetry. The poet breaks the lines where the reader should pause, so the line breaks are part of the poem.
fact: A poet is a person who writes poems.
fact: Pupils read poets in English lessons and learn about rhyme, rhythm and imagery.
fact: Poets paint pictures with words, and the simile, metaphor, personification and alliteration are some of their favourite tricks.
fact: «Free verse» is poetry with no regular rhyme or beat, and the poet decides where each line breaks.
fact: «Ada was the daughter of the poet Lord Byron.» Poet is the word for the person who wrote the poems, so Byron was a poet.
exercise: What is a poet? | A person who sells books | A person who paints pictures on walls | A person who reads newspapers | *A person who writes poems
exercise: In «Poets paint pictures with words», what does paint mean here? | Write the word paint in a book | Make a picture with a brush | *Create pictures in the reader's mind with words | Cover a wall with colour
exercise: «Free verse has no regular rhyme or beat, but the poet breaks the lines where the reader should pause.» Where does the poet break the lines? | Wherever the page is full | Only at the end of each page | *Where the reader should pause | At every full stop
test: Which of these is one of a poet's favourite tricks? | Full stop | Capital letter | Page number | *Alliteration
test: Ada was the daughter of which poet? | Rat | *Lord Byron | Taras Shevchenko | Shakespeare
exam: Which sentence shows a poet at work? | *«Poets paint pictures with words.» | «Please pass the salt.» | «The cat sat on the mat.» | «I went to school today.»
